[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67547,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cystic tumour of the atrioventricular node (CTAVN) is a benign endodermal developmental rest forming a mass lesion in the region of the atrioventricular node.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67548,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8454/0 Cystic tumour of atrioventricular node</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67549,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F01 &amp; XH55F1 Benign neoplasm of intrathoracic organs &amp; Cystic tumour of atrioventricular node</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67550,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> endodermal heterotopia.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> mesothelioma of the atrioventricular node.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67551,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67552,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "<p>CTAVN occurs in the triangle of Koch, within the atrioventricular septum.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T17:48:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67553,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Initially asymptomatic tumours may manifest later in life as the tumours enlarge due to glandular secretions. Symptoms may range from none to palpitations, dyspnoea, syncope, dizziness, partial or complete heart block, and sudden cardiac death.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67554,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CTAVN accounts for about 2.7% of cardiac tumours at autopsy {29221317}. The mean age at diagnosis is about 38&nbsp;years (range: 0&ndash;95&nbsp;years). Women are affected more often than men. No racial or ethnic predilection has been noted.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67555,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CTAVN is thought to be congenital in nature, although its precise etiology is unknown.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67556,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This endodermal rest is believed to occur due to abnormal migration during embryogenesis. About 10% of individuals with CTAVN also have midline developmental defects suggestive of a genetic defect affecting migration of embryological tissues.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67557,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A CTAVN may be apparent as a small bulge or swelling within the atrioventricular septum. The cysts may or may not be apparent grossly and may contain fluid or pultaceous debris.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67558,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cysts are lined by columnar, transitional, or squamous cells. Goblet cells and sebaceous cells have also been described. No cellular atypia is present and mitotic figures are rare.</p>\r\n<p>CTAVN stains with Alcian blue and PAS, exhibiting resistance to both hyaluronidase and diastase digestion. There is positive staining for cytokeratin AE1/AE3, CK5, and CEA. Scattered cells may be positive for serotonin, chromogranin, and calcitonin. Mesothelial, endothelial, and lymphatic markers are negative {31489395}.</p>\r\n<p>On electron microscopy, the cells form solid nests with a basement membranes. Cytoplasmic tonofilaments, desmosomes, electron-dense material, and short microvilli are seen.</p>\r\n<p>Differential diagnoses include simple cysts or bronchogenic cysts and intracardiac teratoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67559,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not described</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67560,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67561,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Endodermal inclusion forming a cystic lesion within the atrioventricular septum</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67562,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67563,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 146,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are usually apparent only at autopsy. Rare cases have been surgically excised. Fatal arrhythmias may occur despite pacemaker placement. There is no correlation between tumour size and occurrence of arrhythmia.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:42:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]